<title>POLAND: Polish 1996 industrial output up yr/yr 10.1 pct. [CORRECTED 17:52 GMT]</title>
<headline>Polish 1996 industrial output up yr/yr 10.1 pct. [CORRECTED 17:52 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's industrial output nadjusted) rose 2.1 percent in December after a 7.1 percent fall in November, and was 10.1 percent higher than in December 1995, the Central Statistical Office  said. The year-on-year rise compared with 1.5 percent (corrects from 10.2 percent) in December 1995.</p>
<p> POLISH INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT    DECEMBER     NOVEMBER     DEC 1995</p>
<p> month/month change (pct)	 2.1	-7.1 (-7.3)    -3.2</p>
<p> yr/yr change (pct)		10.1	 4.7  (4.5)     1.5</p>
<p> index (mthly avge 1994=100)   25.9	 N/A (23.4)   *33.9</p>
<p> mining m/m change		 -0.5	11.3(-10.8)    -7.2</p>
<p> mining yr/yr change	     -2.2	-7.3 (-6.8)   -11.3</p>
<p> manufacturing m/m change	 0.7	-7.9 (-8.2)    -4.7</p>
<p> manufacturing yr/yr change    13.3	 7.3  (7.0)     2.3</p>
<p> utilities m/m change	    15.9	 5.3	     12.3</p>
<p> utilities yr/yr change	  -1.8	-4.7		4.7 @</p>
<p>    NOTES - Revised data in brackets. December 1996, November</p>
<p>1996 and December 1995 all had 21 working days. * December 1995</p>
<p>index is based on a monthly average from 1992.</p>
<p>     -- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
